  "text": "OLUTION:\n1.) Factorize by grouping:\n\t$3z^4-4z^3+5z^2-11z+2= (3z^4-4z^3)+(5z^2-11z+2)$\n\t$= z^3(3z-4)+ 111(5z^2-11z+2)$\n1.) Factorize further:\n\t$=(3z-4)(z^3+5z^2-2)$\n1.) Find the zeros by setting the expression equal to zero:\n\t$(3z-4)(z^3+5z^2-2)=0$\n1) $(3z-4)=0 \\Rightarrow z=\\frac{4}{3}$\n2) $z^3+5z^2-2=0$\n\nNow we solve for $z$ in this equation:\n\t\n2.) Use substitution $w=z+z^2$:\n\t$w^3+6w^2+9w+2-8w^3-12w^2-9w-8=0$\n\t$(w-2)(w^2+8w+4)=0$\n2.1.) Factorize:\n\t$w-2=(w-2)(w-4)$\n2.2.) solve for w:\n\t$(w-2)=0 \\Rightarrow w=2 \\text{ or } (w-4)=0 \\Rightarrow w=4$\n3.) Solve for z using the values of w:\n3.1) w=2:\n\t$z+z^2=2$\n\t$z^2+z-2=0$\n\t$(z-1)(z+2)=0$\n\t$z=1 \\text{ or } z=-2$\n3.2) w=4:\n\t$z+z^2=4$\n\t$z^2+z-4=0$\n\nNow we solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n\t$z=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}$\n3.2.1.) Here,$a=1, b=1,$and$c=-4$. \n\t$z=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{1^2-4(1)(-4)}}{2(1)}$\n\t$z=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$\nTherefore , we have four values for z: 1, -2, $\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{17}}{2}, \\frac{-1-\\sqrt{17}}{2}$\nNow we substitute each value for z into the original expression to confirm:\nCheck $z=\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{17}}{2}$:\n\t$3\\left(\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\right)^4-4\\left(\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\right)^3+5\\left(\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\right)^2-11\\left(\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\right)+2=0$\nCheck $z=\\frac{-1-\\sqrt{17}}{2}$:\n\t$3\\left(\\frac{-1-\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\right)^4-4\\left(\\frac{-1-\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\right)^3+5\\left(\\frac{-1-\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\right)^2-11\\left(\\frac{-1-\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\right)+2=0$\nCheck $z=1$:\n\t$3(1)^4-4(1)^3+5(1)^2-11(1)+2=0$\nCheck $z=-2$:\n\t$3(-2)^4-4(-2)^3+5(-2)^2-11(-2)+2=0$\n\nFinal Answer: The solutions to the equation are $z=\\frac{4}{3}, -2, 1, \\frac{-1+\\sqrt{17}}{2}, \\frac{-1-\\sqrt{17}}{2}$ with boxed answers as follows:\n$\\boxed{z=\\frac{4}{3}}, \\boxed{z=-2}, \\boxed{z=1}$\n1,2,3,4",
